#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The overview page (#369, sublayer 1e): what `factory top` knows, as the data and the rendering of one read-only page:
#   bin/factory-page view   print the view model of one fresh snapshot, as JSON on stdout
#   bin/factory-page html   print the page of one fresh snapshot, as HTML on stdout
# The page shows, in this order: what waits on the Human, each repository's issues (team, step, pull request with its checks, who it waits
# on), each account's five-hour and weekly use with its teams, and today with the load, each row linking to GitHub, with the age of the
# reading. That output is what a snapshot feed to any host would send.
# Read-only: it writes nothing, starts nothing and reads no credential beyond the gh login that `factory top` already uses. Only the view
# model's fields are in its output (bin/lib/page.mjs, viewOf): no process command line, environment, pid, token path or home path, and an
# account by its letter alone; the raw snapshot never is. An unknown verb exits non-zero with the usage line.
# It serves nothing: the hosting is held until the Human picks the host (https://github.com/tuannd9288/factory/issues/369#issuecomment-6598710705).
# Rendering knows no host: bin/lib/page.mjs knows no port, no address and no server, so the page can be served from any host later.
# Run under the Mac mini's `factory` user, it reads only under that home (~/factory-runs, ~/.local/state/factory, the clones), so the macOS
# privacy controls (TCC) that AGENTS.md names for ~/Desktop do not apply.
exec node "$(dirname "$0")/lib/page-cli.mjs" "$@"
